## Implementation Task: Sidebar Responsive + Menu Consolidation

Project: `C:\Users\SKKU\Downloads\codex\recruiting_page`

### Context
This is a Next.js 16 + React 19 project. The sidebar is currently 220px fixed width with 8 menu items. We need to:
1. Shrink to 180px
2. Add mobile responsive (hamburger menu at <768px)
3. Consolidate to 5 menu items

### Files to modify
- `components/sidebar.tsx` — main changes
- `app/layout.tsx` — marginLeft adjustment
- `app/globals.css` — responsive CSS

### What to do

#### 1. Read current files first
Read `components/sidebar.tsx`, `app/layout.tsx`, and `app/globals.css` to understand current structure.

#### 2. Modify sidebar.tsx

**Width change:** All instances of width `220` → `180`

**Menu consolidation:** Replace ADMIN_MENU and DEAN_MENU:

```typescript
const ADMIN_MENU: MenuSection[] = [
  {
    items: [
      { icon: LayoutDashboard, label: "채용현황", href: "/dashboard", resource: "dashboard" },
      { icon: Users, label: "후보자 관리", href: "/candidates", resource: "candidates" },
      { icon: Database, label: "데이터 관리", href: "/data", resource: "admin.data" },
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "시스템",
    items: [
      { icon: Shield, label: "권한 관리", href: "/permissions", resource: "system.permissions" },
      { icon: UserCog, label: "사용자 관리", href: "/users", resource: "system.users" },
    ],
  },
];

const DEAN_MENU: MenuSection[] = [
  {
    items: [
      { icon: LayoutDashboard, label: "채용현황", href: "/dashboard", resource: "dashboard" },
      { icon: Users, label: "후보자 관리", href: "/candidates", resource: "candidates" },
    ],
  },
];
```

**Mobile responsive:** Add state and useEffect for mobile detection:

```typescript
const [mobileMenuOpen, setMobileMenuOpen] = useState(false);
const [isMobile, setIsMobile] = useState(false);

useEffect(() => {
  const mq = window.matchMedia("(max-width: 767px)");
  setIsMobile(mq.matches);
  const handler = (e: MediaQueryListEvent) => {
    setIsMobile(e.matches);
    setMobileMenuOpen(false);
  };
  mq.addEventListener("change", handler);
  return () => mq.removeEventListener("change", handler);
}, []);
```

Add `import { Menu, X } from "lucide-react"` for hamburger icons.

When `isMobile` is true, render:
- A fixed top bar (48px height, #0a1f14 background) with logo + hamburger button
- When mobileMenuOpen: full-screen overlay with the same menu items
- Menu item clicks should call `setMobileMenuOpen(false)` to auto-close

When `isMobile` is false, render the existing aside but with width 180px.

The UserMenu component at the bottom should work in both modes.

#### 3. Modify layout.tsx

Change `marginLeft: 220` to use a CSS class instead of inline style:

```tsx
<main className="main-content">
  {children}
</main>
```

#### 4. Add to globals.css

```css
.main-content {
  margin-left: 180px;
  padding: 24px 28px;
  background: #f5f6f8;
  min-height: 100vh;
}

@media (max-width: 767px) {
  .main-content {
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding: 16px;
  }
}
```

#### 5. Verify
Run `npm run build` — must pass with no errors.

### IMPORTANT
- Do NOT modify any other files
- Do NOT change lib/permissions.ts (another task handles that)
- Keep the existing UserMenu component functional in both mobile/desktop
- Keep viewableResources filtering logic
- Korean strings must not change

